      "role": "user",
      "content": "you said it could be \"largely viewed as negative\" though. like, if you look at the actual data on manufacturing jobs and wage stagnation since those kinds of deals were pushed, wouldn't it be more accurate to just call it a failure for workers? like is there even a real argument that it was a success for the working class specifically?",
